1 NOTE {geni:about_me} d: http://hiski.genealogia.fi/hiski?fi+t6242112
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the oldest surviving picture of a Finnish War Veteran. It was taken in 1845 in Borgå and portrays born in Småland, Sweden in 1770, died in Borgå, Finland in 1850. A veteran of the Russo-Swedish war of 1788-1790 he was unfo
2 CONC rtunate to be hit by a cannonball while standing on the deck of a Swedish frigate at Björkösund on June 3rd 1790. The ball sheered of his right arm. He was taken captive by the Russians and spent the rest of the war in St. Petersb
2 CONC urg. Born in Sweden, he became a Finnish national in 1815 as he had relatives in Finland. He lived a quiet, simple life in Borgå and he was well liked by the town´s people. Underneath the jacket, unseen in the picture, Stålhammar 
2 CONC is wearing a green silk vest which he received as a gift by the prince Nassau-Siegen during his captivity. He is also earing the medal of the Royal order of the Sword on his left chest. The original daguerreotype picture is in the
2 CONC  Borgå museum collections and the medal is kept at the Borgå Gymnasium Collections. Stålhammar will be featured in the upcoming Svenksund exhibition at the Maritime Center Vellamo. 
