1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Johan de Witt==
2 CONT * [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:tmDu5QBuWdoJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_de_Witt+cornelius+fransz+de+witt,+born+1545,+holland&cd=4&hl=en&ct=clnk&lr= about - '''Johan de Witt'''] - Wikipedia - English
2 CONT
2 CONT '''born''' - 24 Sep. 1625, Dordrecht, Netherlands '''died''' - 20 aug 1672, The Hague, Netherlands '''married''' - Wendela Bicker (1635 - 1668) on 16 Feb. 1655 '''children''' - 
2 CONT # Anna de Witt (1655-1725, married to Herman van den Honert
2 CONT # Agnes de Witt (1658-1688, married to Simon Teresteyn van Halewijn
2 CONT # Maria de Witt (1660-1689), married to Willem Hooft
2 CONT # Johan de Witt, Jr. (1662-1701, ''heer van zuid- en Noord- Linschoten, Snelrewaard and IJsselverre'' ,married to Wilhelmina de Witt.  He was secretary of the city of Dordrecht.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan de Witt, heer van Zuid- en Noord-Linschoten, Snelrewaard, Hekenddorp and IJsselverre, was a key figure in Dutch politics in the mid 17th century, when its flourishisng sea trade in a period of globalization made the United P
2 CONC rovinces a leading European power during the '''''Dutch Golden Age'''''.  De Witt controlled the Netherlands political system from around 1650 until shortly before his spectacular death in 1672 working with various factions from n
2 CONC earby all the manor cities, especially his hometown, Dordrecht, and the city of birth of his wife, Amsterdam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan and his older brother Cornelis de Witt, grew up in a privileged social environment in terms of education, his father having as good acquaintances important scholars and scientists, such as ''Isaac Beeckman, Jacob Cats, Gerha
2 CONC rd Vossius and Andreas Colvius''.  Johan and Cornelis both attended the Latin school in Dordrecht. etc...
