1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Philip_Creutz Count '''Gustaf Philip Creutz'''] was a Finland's Swedish statesman, diplomat and poet.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Creutz was born''' in Finland and after concluding his studies at the Royal Academy of Turku he received a post in the Privy Council Chancery at Stockholm in 1751. Here he met [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Fredrik_Gylle
2 CONC nborg Count Gustaf Fredrik Gyllenborg], with whom his name is indissolubly connected. They were closely allied with [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedvig_Charlotta_Nordenflycht Hedvig Charlotta Nordenflycht], and their works, poet
2 CONC ry, were published in common; to their own generation they seemed equal in fame, but posterity has given the palm of genius to Creutz.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His greatest work''' is contained in the 1762 volume, the idyll of '''Atis och Camilla'''; the exquisite little pastoral entitled Daphne was published at the same time, and Gyllenborg was the first to proclaim the supremacy of 
2 CONC his friend.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1763 Creutz''' practically closed his poetical career; he went to Spain as ambassador, and after three years to Paris in the same capacity until May 1783, and it was during this time that Creutz met with the American residen
2 CONC t in Paris at the time, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Franklin Benjamin Franklin]. Creutz and Franklin drafted the first [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Amity_and_Commerce_(United_States%E2%80%93Sweden Treaty of
2 CONC  Amity and Commerce] between the two nations.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1783 King''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_III_of_Sweden Gustav III of Sweden] recalled him and heaped honours upon him, but he died soon after. In 1784, he was elected a member of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
2 CONC Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Sciences Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Atis och Camilla''' was long the most admired poem in the Swedish language; it is written in a spirit of pastoral which is now to some degree faded, but in comparison with most of the other productions of the time it is freshne
2 CONC ss itself. Creutz introduced a melody and grace into the Swedish tongue which it lacked before, and he has been styled the last artificer of the language.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT Franzén, Frans Michael  [http://runeberg.org/fmfdikt/1/0053.html Sång över Greve Gustaf Philip Creutz], prisbelönt med Svenska Akademiens Stora pris 1797.
2 CONT
