1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Beata Drummond was the daughter of a Scottish soldier, Francis Drummond. He served as a soldier in the Swedish army in the first half of the 17th century. He is mentioned in the Swedish sources from around 1636 wh
2 CONC en he served as an ensign in the Kalmar regiment. He rose through the ranks until his death on 22 September 1656 in Neumarkt, Germany. Francis married into Swedish nobility tghrough Kristina Eketrä who became his wife before 1652.
2 CONC  Two daughters, Elisabet and Beata are known. He is mentioned as of noble birth in Swedish judicial records of 1654, but nowhere is it mentioned where he came from in Scotland."
2 CONT
2 CONT == Source ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=6410&id2=6410 Beata Drummond] in Scotland, Scandinavia and Northern European Biographical Database,  (University of St. Andrews), accessed May 22, 2013.
