2 CONT Prior to his immigration to America near the end of his life, predicated upon his reported death on 7 June 1663 at Wyldwick, New York, Claes (Nicholas) De Witt, based on the information provided by A. J. F. Van Laer, resided in Gr
2 CONC oatholdt by Esens in Emberland, which was just a few miles northeast of Emden, the sea port in East Friesland, Netherlands. This East Friesland is not to be confused with the East Friesland in Germany. Please see the notes under T
2 CONC jerck Classen De Witt for further clarification. RAJ   
2 CONT
2 CONT "Nicholaas or Claes De Witt is known to have resided in Grootholt, Oosterbeus & Esens... His wife was Tjeatje Cornelisz, daughter of Cornelis Pieterz..."   (material received 16 August 2001 from Vona E De Witt Smith, 2288 Gale Ave
2 CONC nue, British Columbia, V3K 2Y8, Canada)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File gives the parents of Nicholaes De Witt to be Jan De Witt, born about 1565 and Jacomina Van Barestijne, married on 18 February 1590 in Dordrecht, Zuid Holland, Netherlands. RAJ
2 CONT
