2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died 1699 or 1700
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/M5G4-KBF/tjerck-claessen-dewitt-1620-1701
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/44542669/tjerck_claessen-dewitt
2 CONT
2 CONT Tjerck Claessen DeWitt was born in 1620 in Groatland, Holland to Nicholas C. DeWitt and Tjaatje (VanLeuven) Dewitt Tjerck married Barbara Andriessen on April 24, 1656 in the Reformed Collegiate Dutch Church in New Amsterdam. Tjerc
2 CONC k died on February 17, 1700 at Kingston, Ulster County, New York.
2 CONT *Note
2 CONT dicknlissa@comcast.net
2 CONT Their suggestion:
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT Although Tjerck Claessen DeWitt (1630-1700) is almost certainly buried in the Old Dutch Reformed Church churchyard, the headstone shown on Find A Grave is that of his grandson. The oldest existing headstone for the cemetery is tha
2 CONC t of Tjerck's oldest son, Andries, who died tragically in a building accident in 1710. This stone has been removed to the safety of the church museum, and may be viewed there.
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to all of my sources and the memorial itself, the birthdate s/be 1620 rather than 1630. Kim Hoffman Wilson (KsCityKim) Thanks!!
2 CONT
2 CONT Tjerck and Barbarba DeWitt had a son named Bastiaan DeWitt, born in 1682.
2 CONT Diane
2 CONT ______________________________
2 CONT edit suggestion from Grace;
2 CONT In reading Tjerck DeWitt, b. 1620, will, today, I do not find any child named Bastiaan DeWitt, b. 1682, which Diane has left as a note, in the Bio section on this page.
2 CONT --The will which is found mid-page 29-31 of the "Pawling Genealogy, offered by Ancestry as documentation for the Tjerck Claessen DeWitt Family who married into the Pawling Family.
2 CONT --Also, the other information in this document where the Tjerck will is quoted, says the son of Tjerck -- named Tjerck, b. 1676 in Kingston, Ulster, NY, is the last son born to Tjerck.
2 CONT --Bastiaan DeWitt may be born to another Tjerck DeWitt, but not to this Tjerck Claessen DeWitt, b. 1620-- d. Feb 17, 1700 and his wife Barbara.
