1 NAME Emmerentje Claessen /de Witt/
2 GIVN Emmerentje Claessen
2 SURN de Witt
2 _MARNM Hoffman
2 NICK Emmerens
2 NICK Emerensje
2 NICK Ammereus
2 NICK Emerentje
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1647
2 ADDR
3 CITY Grootholdt
3 STAE Ostfriesland
3 CTRY Heiliges Römisches Reich Deutscher Nation
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1688
2 ADDR
3 STAE New York
1 OCCU
1 TITL 2 rd wife
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Emmerentje Claessen and her brother Jan Claessen, appear to have accompanied there sister Ida Claessen de Witt van Steenwyck when the van Steenwycks returned to New Netherland on '''''the passenger ship "de Vos" '
2 CONC '''', that sailed from Amsterdam after 31 August 1662 and arrived at New Amsterdam on 14 Nov. 1662. The following passengers are on the passenger list:
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://www.geni.com/people/Jan-Albertsen/6000000019786154913 '''''Jan Albantsen, from Steenwyck'''''], and Wife and child. This would be the Jan, Ida and infant daughter, that were murdered at Esopus, Ulster, NN during the Indi
2 CONC an raid on Jun 7, 1663.
2 CONT *Ammereus Claesen, maiden. This would be '''Emmerentje'''; she married Marten Hermanzen Hoffman at New Amsterdam on May 16, 1664.
2 CONT *Hendrick Albertsen; :Labourer. This is interesting, could this Hendrick be a relative of Jan Albertsen Steenwyck?
2 CONT *Jan Claesen; labourer, This would be brother Jan Claessen that settled in Ulster, NY and died unmarried.
2 CONT **Also on that voyage there were a fellow passengers "Roelof Hermansen, from Germany, and Wife." Could this have been a brother to Marten Hermanzen. If so, it would provide another clue to the marriage of Emmerentje and Marten.<br
2 CONC />
2 CONT
2 CONT Marten arrived at New Netherland in 1657, settled at Esopus, Ulster, NN; then moved to New Amsterdam. According to the City directory, he lived on de Here Straat (now Broadway). He resided in New Amsterdam and in Albany.[4] He als
2 CONC o dwelt at Brooklyn, Kings, New York, USA. By 1678 he removed to Kingston, Ulster, New York. He received a grant of "Crown Land" in the town of Kingston, Ulster, NY on February 7, 1688[5].
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unfortunate that the Genealogy of The Hoffman Family begins with Marten."
2 CONT
